<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n96311" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στᾰφῠλ-ή</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bunch of grapes</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σταφυλῇσι μέγα βρίθουσαν ἀλωήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					18.561
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμερὶς ἡβώωσα τεθήλει δὲ σταφυλῇσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					5.69
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				7.121
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σταφυλαὶ παντοῖαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					24.343
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				844e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Apoc.</u>
				14.18
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πυρναίαις ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				1.46
			</span></i>; of ripe, fresh grapes, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄμφαξ</span> on the one hand, and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σταφίς</span> on the other, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				5.303
			</span></i>: collectively in sg., <i><span class="en">
				<u>PPetr.</u>
				3p.60
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
				300.14
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				116.18
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. ἀγρία</span>,= 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήλωθρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				3.18.11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plin.
				<u>HN</u>
				23.21
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>uvula when swollen at the end so as to resemble a grape</i> on
			the stalk, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Prog.</u>
				23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nicopho
				28
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				493a3
			</span></i>; of the <i>uvula</i> generally, <i><span class="en">
				Archig.
			</span></i> ap.<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				12.969
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				974
			</span></i>; <i>inflammation of the uvula,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				42(1).126.30
			</span></i> (Epid, <span class="entity">ii A.D.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				7.731
			</span></i> (pl.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			parox. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σταφύλη</span>, <i>plummet of a
				level</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵπποι . . σταφύλῃ ἐπὶ
				νῶτον ἔϊσαι</span> horses equal in height even <i>by the
				level</i>, matched to a nicety, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.765
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				159
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">Hsch.,
					<u>EM</u>742.44</span></i>.</div>
